# More general scratch/diagnostic captures
*.txt
!Docs/QUICKSTART.txt
# Accessibility-tree snapshot baselines. These are reviewed artifacts, not captures: updating one
# is meant to be a decision someone sees in a diff. The blanket *.txt above had been swallowing
# them, so a baseline could go stale and no reviewer could tell — which is exactly what happened
# when the governance sidebar was reworked and its baseline kept describing the old menu.
!tests/ETL-SQL.Portal.BrowserTests/Snapshots/*.snapshot.txt
# Browser type-gate baseline. Same trap a third time: this file is the gate's entire memory of
# what was already broken, so a checkout without it reports all 681 known findings as new.
!/browser-typecheck-baseline.txt
# Reporting golden terminal renders. Same reasoning, same trap: the blanket *.txt above swallowed
# every one of them on the commit that introduced the lane, so the artifacts passed locally and
# were absent on a fresh checkout. The lane fails when a hash matches but its artifact is missing,
# which is how that was caught.
!tests/fixtures/reporting/goldens/**/terminal.txt
*.cs.scratch
*.etlsql.scratch

# Transient cert-run logs (baseline-*.json and cert-report.* stay tracked)
certification-results/*.log
certification-results/*.err
certification-results/*.out
certification-results/baseline-*-runs/
certification-results/commit-comparison/
# Local HA/enterprise certification evidence is retained for release packaging, not source control.
certification-results/enterprise-hardening/
# Deployment-profile lanes write a timestamped bundle per run. Release evidence goes to
# artifacts/release-evidence/<version>/ via -ReleaseVersion (already ignored); a local run is
# development evidence and is never release eligible, so it does not belong in source control.
certification-results/deployment-profiles/
certification-results/postgres-ha-soak/ha-overnight-*/
certification-results/ha-large-job-soak/ha-overnight-*/
certification-results/ha-fault-injection/ha-overnight-*/
# Gate F keeps one compact, reproducible report; child logs, keys, and status are run-local.
certification-results/gate-f-1b/*
!certification-results/gate-f-1b/gate-f-report.json
test_lineage.md
test_out.txt
tests_list.txt

